lQ29tbWVudDQ0NTcwMDMwNw==","user":{"login":"mc-zone","id":4403937,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDM5Mzc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4403937?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mc-zone","html_url":"https://github.com/mc-zone","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mc-zone/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mc-zone/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mc-zone/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mc-zone/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mc-zone/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mc-zone/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mc-zone/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mc-zone/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mc-zone/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2018-12-10T06:18:47Z","updated_at":"2018-12-10T06:18:47Z","body":"@sokra We can also change `webpack-dev-middleware` to use [`compiler.run(callback)`](https://github.com/webpack/webpack/blob/master/lib/Compiler.js#L207)(finalCallback) instead of the `done` hook to figure out that the compilation has finished?\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/webpack/webpack/blob/d5e26f728adb63a1fca080ef728fd627952a921d/lib/Compiler.js#L207-L211\r\n\r\nIn `webpack-dev-middleware`, using:\r\n```javascript\r\ncompiler.run(finished);\r\n```\r\n\r\nInstead of:\r\n```javascript\r\ncompiler.hooks.done.tap('WebpackDevMiddleware', finished);\r\n```\r\n\r\nOr you consider that add an `afterDone` hook is more elegant? \r\n\r\nI'd like to make PR of this, just want to make sure which way is more sensible.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack/issues/comments/445700307/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"perfor